<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via overnight system RP's.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via overnight system RP's.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added reserves to the banking system Wednesday via overnight system repurchase agreements, a Fed spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The move was mostly in line with the market's expectations.</p>
<p>At 1130 EDT/1530 GMT, the time the Fed ususally intervenes in the market, the fed funds rate was quoted at 5-1/4 percent, in line with the central bank's target.</p>
<p>--Amanda Stultz, 212-859-1600</p>
</text>
